/// Category of a farm operating expense (RAKHAL-348, Purchasing —
/// `FINANCE_V2_DESIGN.md` §5.1). Deliberately restricted to exactly the
/// **non-Purchase** expense ledger accounts RAKHAL-333 already seeded
/// (`finance-v2/ledger/domain/default-chart-of-accounts.ts`, 5xxx range):
/// `SALARY` (5200), `UTILITIES` (5400, the design doc's own worked example —
/// "an electricity bill is an expense"), `BREEDING` (5300), `TRANSFER_FEE`
/// (5500), `DEPRECIATION` (5600).
///
/// **`FEED` (5000) / `MEDICINE` (5100) are deliberately excluded** — a feed or
/// medicine purchase is a `Purchase` (increases the Inventory asset), never an
/// `Expense`, per this ticket's own core split (`FINANCE_V2_DESIGN.md` §5.1:
/// "a feed purchase increases an asset, an electricity bill is an expense —
/// not both recorded as generic expense"). Those two seeded expense-category
/// ledger accounts exist for a different, later purpose (e.g. RAKHAL-351/352's
/// per-animal/report cost bucketing), not for this model.
///
/// **No `OTHER` value** — unlike Revenue's `4900 Other Income`
/// (`IncomeCategory`/`OtherIncome`, RAKHAL-350), RAKHAL-333's seeded chart has
/// no catch-all "Other Expense" ledger account in the 5xxx range. Adding an
/// `OTHER` category here would have nothing real to post against without
/// editing `default-chart-of-accounts.ts` — out of this ticket's lane
/// (`finance-v2/ledger/**` is RAKHAL-333/334's read-only lane). Flagged as
/// `RD-060` in `TECH_DEBT.md` for a future ticket to add a seeded `5900 Other
/// Expense` account and extend this enum additively.
enum ExpenseCategory {
  SALARY
  UTILITIES
  BREEDING
  TRANSFER_FEE
  DEPRECIATION

  /// RAKHAL-367 (MILESTONE 22) — the catch-all this doc comment's own
  /// "No `OTHER` value" note flagged as RD-060. Posts against the newly
  /// seeded `5900 Other Expense` ledger account
  /// (`finance-v2/ledger/domain/default-chart-of-accounts.ts`). Closes
  /// RD-060.
  OTHER
}

/// RAKHAL-367 (MILESTONE 22, `BUSINESS_IA_PRD.md` §9.4) — a `Purchase` has no
/// `PATCH` that changes money on a posted document (journal immutability,
/// RAKHAL-334 AC 3); the only correction is void + re-record. `Sale` already
/// has this concept (`SaleStatus.CANCELLED`/`REFUNDED`) — `Purchase` needed
/// its own since it has no status column at all today. The actual void route
/// + reversal cascade is RAKHAL-377's job; this ticket only adds the column.
enum PurchaseStatus {
  CONFIRMED
  VOIDED
}
